@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+"@elata-biosciences/rppg-web": minor
+---
+
+With face tracking on (`face_mesh` mode without an explicit `roi`), drop a frame with no face (drop reason `no_face`, `roiSource` null, no `onStats` call) instead of reading a 100x100 square at the centre of the frame; after two seconds without a face, report no reading from `RppgSession.getMetrics()` (every estimate cleared as for a failed backend, reason `no_face`, baseline and calibration state kept), and when the face returns, restart the fuser, the sample window and the engine pipeline. Add the `requireFace` option (on by default in that mode; `false` keeps the previous behaviour), `DemoRunner.faceAbsentMs()`, `RppgProcessor.resetSignal()` and the `no_face` member of `DemoRunnerDropReason` (an exhaustive switch over it needs a case). `video_frame` mode and an explicit `roi` are unchanged.
diff --git a/packages/rppg-web/README.md b/packages/rppg-web/README.md
index 9a34403..da00c1a 100644
--- a/packages/rppg-web/README.md
+++ b/packages/rppg-web/README.md
@@ -319,6 +319,20 @@ contains `insufficient_window`. Once that clears, the processor has enough
 samples for a BPM estimate. `diagnostics.windowSampleCount` gives the raw
 sample count if you want to show a progress indicator.
 
+**No face, no reading:** in `face_mesh` mode (without an explicit `roi`), a frame
+in which the face finder found no face is dropped (`lastDropReason: "no_face"`,
+`roiSource: null`, no `onStats` call) instead of being read from the centre of
+the frame. After two seconds with no face, `session.getMetrics()` reports no
+reading: `bpm: null`, `confidence: 0` and every other estimate cleared as for a
+failed backend, with reason code `no_face`; the rolling baseline and calibration
+state are kept. A shorter miss keeps the last reading. When the face returns
+after those two seconds, the sample window and the engine pipeline start afresh, so
+the window's estimates use only frames from after the gap. A number comes back
+within a few seconds; the first ones come from a short window and can be off by
+several bpm until it fills. The Bayesian tracker, the rate history, calibration
+and the baseline carry over. Pass `requireFace: false` to keep the
+previous behaviour; `video_frame` mode and an explicit `roi` are unchanged.
+
 **FaceMesh fallback:** `faceMesh: "auto"` falls back to `video_frame` mode if
 MediaPipe fails to load. Check `diagnostics.faceTrackingMode` to see which
 mode is active — `"face_mesh"` or `"video_frame"`.
